---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Choose between recording transcription and Android voice-keyboard dictation, then find setup and troubleshooting guidance."
>
  <section class="section intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Voice Inbox documentation</p>
    <h1>Choose how you want to use Voice Inbox.</h1>
    <p>
      Process accumulated recordings into a searchable text inbox on Android or iOS, or use the
      Android-only Voice Inbox keyboard for short phrases directly inside an editable field.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/setup/`}>Open setup guide</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}/docs/voice-keyboard/`}>Set up voice keyboard</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}/faq/`}>Browse FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Recordings workflow</p>
        <h2>Process audio into your inbox</h2>
        <p>Install a compatible model, create or select an output document, import recordings, preview them, and transcribe individually or in a batch.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/setup/`}>Read the setup guide →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Android dictation</p>
        <h2>Dictate a short phrase in any app</h2>
        <p>Enable the compact Voice Inbox keyboard, prepare its local model, and insert recognized text into the active editor.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/docs/voice-keyboard/`}>Read the voice-keyboard guide →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Get answers</h2>
        <p>Find help with device requirements, audio files, model installation, transcripts, and failures.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/faq/`}>Read the FAQ →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Join testing</h2>
        <p>Voice Inbox for Android is currently distributed through Google Play closed testing.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/testing/`}>Read testing instructions →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>Learn how local transcription, downloaded models, and selected files work.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>Read privacy information →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Legal and acknowledgements</h2>
        <p>Review app information, source licensing, third-party notices, and model attribution.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/legal/`}>Read legal information →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section note">
    <h2>Platform notes</h2>
    <p>
      Android includes individual imports and sharing, optional folder processing, scheduled transcription,
      and the Android-only voice keyboard. The iOS MVP supports app-local, shared, and selected-folder imports,
      preview, batch transcription, transcript review, output append, and startup processing while the app is
      active. Scheduled or background transcription is not available on iOS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .intro { max-width: 760px; }
    .intro h1 { margin-bottom: 22px; }
    .intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; }
    .card h2 { font-size: 1.18rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
